   - Need additional test for total precision
   
2. Empty items validation mutation survived
   - Missing edge case test
*/
```

## Test-Driven Development (TDD)

### TDD Cycle

Red-Green-Refactor là core cycle của TDD:

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                      TDD Cycle                                   │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                                  │
│  1. RED Phase                                                   │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │  Write a failing test that describes the desired         │   │
│  │  behavior. The test should fail for the right reason.    │   │
│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │
│                              │                                   │
│                              ▼                                   │
│  2. GREEN Phase                                                 │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │  Write the minimum code necessary to make the test       │   │
│  │  pass. Don't worry about perfect code, just make it      │   │
│  │  work.                                                   │   │
│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │
│                              │                                   │
│                              ▼                                   │
│  3. REFACTOR Phase                                             │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │  Improve the code while keeping tests passing.           │   │
│  │  Remove duplication, improve naming, simplify logic.     │   │
│  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │
│                              │                                   │
│                              ▼                                   │
│                         Repeat...                                │
│                                                                  │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### TDD Workflow

1. Write failing test (Red)
2. Run test to verify failure
3. Write minimal code (Green)
4. Run test to verify pass
5. Refactor code (Refactor)
6. Run tests to verify
7. Repeat

### TDD Example

```typescript
// STEP 1: Write failing test (Red)
describe('Money', () => {
    describe('add', () => {
        it('should add two money values with same currency', () => {
            const m1 = new Money(100, Currency.USD);
            const m2 = new Money(50, Currency.USD);

            const result = m1.add(m2);

            expect(result.amount).toBe(150);
            expect(result.currency).toBe(Currency.USD);
        });
    });
});

// Test fails: Money class doesn't exist yet

// STEP 2: Write minimal code (Green)
class Money {
    constructor(
        public readonly amount: number,
        public readonly currency: Currency
    ) {}

    add(other: Money): Money {
        return new Money(this.amount + other.amount, this.currency);
    }
}

// Test passes

// STEP 3: Add more tests
it('should throw when adding different currencies', () => {
    const m1 = new Money(100, Currency.USD);
    const m2 = new Money(50, Currency.EUR);

    expect(() => m1.add(m2)).toThrow(CurrencyMismatchException);
});

// Test fails: No currency check

// STEP 4: Refactor
class Money {
    constructor(
        public readonly amount: number,
        public readonly currency: Currency
    ) {}

    add(other: Money): Money {
        if (!this.currency.equals(other.currency)) {
            throw new CurrencyMismatchException(this.currency, other.currency);
        }
        return new Money(this.amount + other.amount, this.currency);
    }
}

// All tests pass
```

### Test Naming Conventions

```typescript
// Test naming pattern: describe + it
describe('OrderAggregate', () => {
    describe('addItem', () => {
        it('should add item to draft order', () => {
            // Test implementation
        });

        it('should throw error when adding item to confirmed order', () => {
            // Test implementation
        });
    });

    describe('confirm', () => {
        it('should confirm order with items and valid payment', () => {
            // Test implementation
        });

        it('should throw error when confirming empty order', () => {
            // Test implementation
        });
    });
});

// BDD-style naming
describe('Order Creation', () => {
    scenario('customer can create order with valid items', () => {
        given('a customer with valid cart items');
        when('they submit order');
        then('order should be created with status DRAFT');
    });

    scenario('customer cannot create empty order', () => {
        given('a customer with empty cart');
        when('they submit order');
        then('error should be returned');
    });
});
```

### TDD Coverage Strategy

```
                    ┌──────────────┐
                    │     E2E      │  5-10% (few, critical flows)
                    │    Tests     │
                    ├──────────────┤
                    │  Integration │  20-30% (API, DB interactions)
                    │    Tests     │
                    ├──────────────┤
                    │   Unit       │  60-70% (business logic)
                    │   Tests      │
                    └──────────────┘
```

| Layer | Coverage Target |
|-------|-----------------|
| Domain Layer | 100% |
| Application Layer | 90% |
| Infrastructure Layer | 70% |

### Test Data Builders

```typescript
class OrderBuilder {
    private id: OrderId = OrderId.generate();
    private customerId: CustomerId = new CustomerId('default-customer');
    private items: OrderItem[] = [];
    private status: OrderStatus = OrderStatus.DRAFT;

    withId(id: OrderId): this {
        this.id = id;
        return this;
    }

    withCustomer(customerId: CustomerId): this {
        this.customerId = customerId;
        return this;
    }

    withItem(product: Product, quantity: number): this {
        this.items.push(OrderItem.create(product, new Quantity(quantity)));
        return this;
    }

    withStatus(status: OrderStatus): this {
        this.status = status;
        return this;
    }

    build(): Order {
        const order = Order.create(this.customerId, testAddress());
        for (const item of this.items) {
            order.addItem(item.product, item.quantity);
        }
        if (this.status === OrderStatus.CONFIRMED) {
            order.confirm('pay-123');
        }
        return order;
    }
}

// Usage in tests
describe('Order Tests', () => {
    it('should calculate total correctly', () => {
        const order = new OrderBuilder()
            .withCustomer(new CustomerId('cust-123'))
            .withItem(testProduct('A', 100), 2)
            .withItem(testProduct('B', 50), 1)
            .build();

        expect(order.total.amount).toBe(250);
    });
});
```

### Test Selection Priority

1. Start with happy path
2. Add edge cases
3. Add error cases
4. Add boundary conditions
5. Test critical paths

